        "date_published": "2026-08-02T07:00:00+00:00",
        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/79c9955b-ce67-4b09-a071-4da0f7db49e6,1785519224090/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%28149%2C270%2C4090%2C2300%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A family poses with a sign that says &apos;JASPER&apos; with mountains in the background' width='620' height='349' title='A family from Switzerland takes a photo at the Jasper sign.'/><p>Though most of the national park has reopened after the Jasper wildfire, a few iconic areas require more extensive repairs that the federal government is backing with an over $500M investment.</p>",
