        "date_published": "2026-08-02T04:00:00+00:00",
        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/7f2dff52-3aa1-4792-a163-3c558d80ddea,1785535605343/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C85%2C4500%2C2531%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='The fins of several orcas stick out of the water.' width='620' height='349' title='In this Jan. 18, 2014, file photo, endangered orcas from the J-pod swim in Puget Sound west of Seattle, as seen from a federal research vessel that had been tracking the whales.'/><p>The Trump administration is being sued by conservation groups over a change they say will weaken habitat protection for endangered species. In Canada, experts say the move could also harm animals that move between the two countries, including migratory birds and southern resident killer whales.</p>",
        "id": 6094399,
