    {
        "age": null,
        "album": "",
        "author": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "comments": [],
        "date_created": "2026-08-02T08:57:03.284036+00:00",
        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-08-02T04:00:00+00:00",
        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/1.4751685,1706046474000/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C157%2C3000%2C1687%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Yellow powder and rocks known as uranium yellowcake, a by-product of uranium production.' width='620' height='349' title='Uranium concentrate is now linked to a digital token and has been trading in the cryptocurrency market since November thanks to the efforts of Canada&apos;s Madison Metals and its partners. Uranium is used in nuclear power plants.'/><p>Canada built its nuclear industry around Candu reactors supplied by a made-in-Canada supply chain. Ontario is building, and other provinces are considering, SMRs that require foreign uranium enrichment and fabrication in an abrupt departure from decades of self-reliance.</p>",
        "id": 6094396,
